  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilient Futures &#x2013; Strengthening Institutional Capacities to Ensure Sustainable Livelihoods in the Region of Tangier-Tetouan-Al Hoceima</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the past decade, the Tangier-Tetouan-Al Hoceima region has experienced numerous natural disasters, including wildfires and floods, causing substantial damage to infrastructure and agriculture. With the support of the Chancellery and Foreign Affairs of Flanders, IOM aims to aid the Moroccan government in planning sustainable adaptation solutions for vulnerable communities in this region. The project focuses on enhancing institutional capacity at both national and regional levels to address climate change, rural poverty, and human mobility while involving Civil Society Organizations (CSOs). Additionally, it aims to build resilience and adaptive capacities in communities at risk of forced migration due to climate change and natural hazards, particularly among women.</narrative>
  </description>
